description: Forbid outline-tracing animations for the stroke drain effect
alwaysApply: true
---

# No outline mode for stroke drain

The stroke drain animation draws each letter down its **centerline** (medial axis / skeleton). Outline tracing — animating the contour of a glyph with `stroke-dashoffset` — is the wrong shape and was deliberately removed.

Do not propose, implement, or reason about outline-tracing approaches for the drain animation. Do not suggest "we could also stroke the outline" as an alternative. The decision is final.

See `plans/stroke-drain-any-font.md` for the centerline approach.

## What "outline mode" means here

Taking the glyph's outline path from `opentype.js`, splitting subpaths, and animating dashoffset around the contour. Example of what NOT to do:

```ts
// BAD: traces the outside of the letter
const reindexed = reindexForDirection(path.commands, direction);
const parts = splitSubpaths(reindexed);
for (const part of parts) {
  // ... animate stroke-dashoffset around the outline
}
```

## What to do instead

Extract centerline polylines from the glyph and animate dashoffset along each polyline. See `plans/stroke-drain-any-font.md`.

If a true centerline extractor isn't available yet, use the clip-rect wipe currently in `src/components/DrainText.tsx` as the placeholder. Never reintroduce outline tracing.
